        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.51,
            0.881,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "**In each case, the angles are the multiples of the smallest angle. You may wonder and ask if this will always happen. What do you think?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.557,
            0.881,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Yes, the angles of symmetry are always the multiples of the smallest angle. For example, the second angle is twice the amount of rotation of the first rotation."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.626,
            0.147,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_35_image_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.628,
            0.276,
            0.648
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "True or False"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.659,
            0.698,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": "• **Every figure will have 360 degrees as an angle of symmetry.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.678,
            0.882,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "**If the smallest angle of symmetry of a figure is a natural number in degrees, then it is a factor of 360.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.723,
            0.284,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** True"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.75,
            0.284,
            0.766
          ],
          "content": "True"
        },
